        <div class="about-bio-tile" aria-label="Professional profile">
          <p class="about-bio-tile-text">Claudio Cammarano leads marketing at De Agostini Libri and is co-founder of Irene Media. With twenty years of experience in Italy's leading publishing groups, he has led editorial marketing, brand positioning and digital transformation strategies. He took part in some of the turning points of Italian publishing, from the joint book-and-newspaper sales of Repubblica to the <em>Fifty Shades</em> phenomenon and the acquisition of Rizzoli by Mondadori. University lecturer at Università Cattolica di Milano, Master Co.Se (Università di Parma) and Università degli Studi di Bergamo; formerly at Scuola Holden. Author of <em>Il mercato del libro</em> (Solferino / Scuola Holden). Academic background in semiotics and philosophy of language; MBA from Hult International Business School.</p>
        </div>

